              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Krisykatt"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I think this recipe is fantastic with one big alteration - add NO water. It tastes great without it and it becomes way too watery with the water. This is one of my staple dressings."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Trillian"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I omitted the water entirely, and substituted corn starch for the xanthan gum. This is a great dressing for a simple green salad that includes iceberg and/or butter lettuce, red onion and fresh Mandarin orange sections. and grilled chicken. Thanks for a great recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2025-08-14T02:25:54.854Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "PeggySue"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Yummy! I left out the water and xantham gum, and cut the salt by half. I didn't bother with the blender, just shook for a few minutes and then let it set overnight for the flavors to blend. Sweet, tangy, and spicy.",
            "datePublished": "2016-04-07T12:26:53.730Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lynnae Haerle Burns"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Instead of using celery seed and regular salt, I added celery salt. I did not add xanthan gum and used a mix of sesame oil and grape seed oils. I added less water than it called for and think next time I will omit water and add avacado. Yum!",
            "datePublished": "2015-08-17T07:11:01.307Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "kellieann"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was really good. I only used 1/4 cup of water and it came out perfect.",
            "datePublished": "2012-04-11T19:52:52.807Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "2"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Goody2shz"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This tasted good but it's very far from being thick and creamy......watery is more like it. That said, I would probably make this again, but only when I'm dieting because it's only 57 calories per 1/8 cup serving, which is a very decent amount of dressing. I'd love to give this more stars for taste, but I'm only giving it two because as written it's deceptive. UPDATE: I tried this again using a bit of xantham gum as a thickener (which I got in bulk at Winco) and that did the trick. Fix the recipe and I'll give it more stars.",
            "datePublished": "2011-04-14T17:45:46.037Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "turkscaicos diane"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Tastes good, but by no means is it creamy. Actually it's very watery. With 1/3 cup vinegar, 3/4 cup water and only 1/3 cup vegetable oil, can't imagine it can become creamy.",
